  "text": "Title: Common knowledge — Examples\n\n\"Paris is the capital of France.\" Many capital cities of developed countries \nare considered common knowledge by most people, but one cannot claim this as \ncommon knowledge for global populations without further research. \"It is dangerous to mix ammonia and bleach.\" \nThough both common household chemicals, accidents involving the mixing of ammonia and bleach are rare,\nbecause the potentially lethal danger in their chemical reaction is a widely circulated cautionary tale amongst some\n  American families and so could possibly be considered common knowledge in those populations, but may not extend to wider populations.",
